{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/647250-so-what-is-mummy-about","id":647250,"title":"So... what is Mummy about?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-31T15:09:52-07:00","id":647250,"title":"So... what is Mummy about?","content":"Hello <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Lately, I decided to come back to NWoD games and was wondering about purchasing Mummy: the Curse. There certainly are things that seem interesting about this game... The thing is, I'm wondering: what is the game about (aside from being about mummies, obviously)?<br /> <br /> Specifically: what is there for the mummies to do in this game? I mean, they wake up and... do what, exactly? What could their stories be about? From what I've read, mummies wake up to hunt down artifacts - but is it all they do? Admittedly, it sounds a bit... limited. Is it all what there is to the game, or am I misinformed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T15:19:10-07:00","id":647277,"title":"","content":"Hunt artifacts, get into turf wars, fight chimeric abominations full of bees, and generally fulfil the demands of ancient gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T15:41:28-07:00","id":647326,"title":"","content":"Tell me more about the &quot;demands of ancient gods&quot; part <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> What could the Judges demand from mummies, exactly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T15:59:16-07:00","id":647340,"title":"","content":"Mummies have mortal cults, so they can be involved in literally anything mortals would consider important. It's a game dealing with themes of slavery. The cult worships the Mummy, but the Mummy is bound to serve the cult (and the gods). In a nutshell, you are woken and compelled to follow a mission. That mission could be anything from helping to expand the cult's corporate interests by a &quot;hostile&quot; takeover, to exploring ancient ruins in search of mystic artefacts. The game can swing between Conan, Lovecraft, and political thriller on a dime. A pulpy sequence involving an epic battle against a chimera flows easily into ruminations on existential horror as you consider the nature of the beings you serve, but before long you can be back blackmailing the corporate overlords of a rival cult into submitting to your influence. That sort of thing.<br /> <br /> And yes, you also hunt artefacts, but your driving purpose can be just about anything (and the default setting, the Sothic Turn, gives you free will in pursuing your own ambitions).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T16:30:22-07:00","id":647354,"title":"","content":"For my group, we focus a lot on the self discovery and memory themes of the game. Tbh in all of this time with the game, we have only done ONE artifact based story, and it wwasn't a treasure hunt or tomb raid, but rather the story of the Blue Beetle was focused more on how it interacts with the host. The rest of the Mummy stuff we've done involves flashbacks to old romance, old rivalries, and old ideas of rebellion. I admit, I probably overplayed the tragic Curse that mummies suffer from, because my players now equate Judges to evil. As storyteller, I should've played that card much later on, because all the Mummies are viewing all NPC mummies as potential threats. Either way, its an exciting and mystifying game. I mean, just sit and stare at a globe for a while. YYou'll see places you'd love to explore, remember history, and all of this becomes storyline. I've never STed a game where the ideas come so naturally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T16:43:57-07:00","id":647361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/647250-so-what-is-mummy-about?p=647326#post647326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tell me more about the &quot;demands of ancient gods&quot; part <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> What could the Judges demand from mummies, exactly?</div> </div> </div> </div>Every Judge has a crime as its purview. They tend to reward Mummies who punish those who commit that crime. Of course, both the crimes and the punishments are very much rooted in Bronze Age culture, so things can get kind of morally odd from a modern perspective very quickly.<br /> <br /> And of course, the Judges like relics, hate Amkhata and Shuankhsen, and are presented as vaguely rapacious (by which I mean that they seek to have relics sent to Duat, diminishing the magic that remains in the world in the process). Personally, I present them as distant more than evil, but they should always be there hanging over the players' heads. Many actions can see the player characters punished by their Judges, and when and why that occurs can be a big moment for the character in question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T17:55:26-07:00","id":647459,"title":"","content":"Okay then! I admit that all of this sounds rather interesting. Thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T05:38:01-07:00","id":648758,"title":"","content":"So, I decided that I'd be very keen on hearing more on the possible Mummy story ideas and the like <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> To get a better feel of the game and all that.<br /> <br /> Anyone interested in sharing some more? I have a few bucks to spare on NWoD books and I need to decide whether I'd like to purchase Mummy first, or go with some Mage supplements, or maybe something else <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T06:22:52-07:00","id":648831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/647250-so-what-is-mummy-about?p=648758#post648758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I decided that I'd be very keen on hearing more on the possible Mummy story ideas and the like <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> To get a better feel of the game and all that.<br /> <br /> Anyone interested in sharing some more? I have a few bucks to spare on NWoD books and I need to decide whether I'd like to purchase Mummy first, or go with some Mage supplements, or maybe something else <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there's already a thread like that in this very forum: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/11948-1001-mummy-story-hooks\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...my-story-hooks</a><br /> <br /> Christian A has started several of these threads for many of the gamelines here and on RPG.net.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, here's a really handy thread where a user is reading through the core book and taking notes. It should give you a better idea of things and potentially help clarify questions that you might have: <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?753149-Mummy-the-Curse-Where-I-Read-the-corebook\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?...d-the-corebook</a>.<br /> <br /> The core book itself has an adventure in the back, Eve of Judgment. It's a quick little story about the meret (mummy party) being awoken in the slums of Brazil to protect their cults from an imminent threat, then investigating why the cults were being attacked and where the final NPC member of the party disappeared to. It has a fantastic ending.<br /> <br /> An idea that I want to see in a game:<br /> <br /> The PCs awaken to find their cults in disarray and schisming. There are signs that another mummy has been trying to suborn the cults and stealing relics. No matter how hard the PCs try, though, they can't seem to find this mysterious mummy. Until at the highlight of the game, they discover the truth: the mystery mummy is actually one of them, or rather their orders from a previous descent. The cults broke into an orthodox/radical split based on some vague language you used and ended up almost tearing your cult apart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":1923,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","user":"BigDamnHero","date":".  Forgot an important word. 09-02-2015, 09:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T14:42:48-07:00","id":649329,"title":"","content":"Thanks, that's very useful <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Here's a question I'm wondering about when trying to wrap my head around this game: the mummies' time is limited, right? Eventually, all of them return to their sleep. So, how long does it take for that to happen? How much time do mummies have in each activity cycle? Days, weeks, months, years..?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T14:57:50-07:00","id":649344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/647250-so-what-is-mummy-about?p=649329#post649329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks, that's very useful <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Here's a question I'm wondering about when trying to wrap my head around this game: the mummies' time is limited, right? Eventually, all of them return to their sleep. So, how long does it take for that to happen? How much time do mummies have in each activity cycle? Days, weeks, months, years..?</div> </div> </div> </div>The timer varies, seeing as it's based on the gradual diminishment of their Sekhem (which serves as their Supernatural Tolerance stat like Blood Potency or Wyrd) and there are ways to spend, regain, or rapidly lose Sekhem, and Sothic Turns in particular are notable for not having a time-based cutoff once the character's Sekhem has dropped to 1.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, though, even a mummy who's completed their objective (and thus automatically succeeds at all further time-based rolls that must be failed to retain Sekhem) can push on for a little under a year (or the length of a couple stories) over the course of dropping from Sekhem 5 to Sekhem 0.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T15:13:44-07:00","id":649357,"title":"","content":"Interesting! So, I wonder... what could a mummy be doing in such limited time? What kind of objectives could they be following, after their appointed mission is completed?<br /> <br /> BTW. How often do mummies rise - can they be called up by their cults every year, for once?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T15:21:05-07:00","id":649362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/647250-so-what-is-mummy-about?p=649357#post649357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting! So, I wonder... what could a mummy be doing in such limited time? What kind of objectives could they be following, after their appointed mission is completed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally speaking, at least some of the spare time the Arisen get is spent on getting up to date with guild politics or handling personal pursuits, particularly as their Memory increases across the centuries.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> BTW. How often do mummies rise - can they be called up by their cults every year, for once? </div> </div> </div>It varies, but mummies can tell their cults to summon them at a certain time or in the event of specific occurrences, and depending on what the cult has at their disposal they may well be able to bring their core demigod out into the land of the living with some regularity; the big obstacles there are the general need for a purpose to the call and the drawbacks of Sybaris, along with the high probability that most cults won't have a relic that personally belonged to the mummy they serve and thus will have to resort to methods like permanently draining vessels or major sacrifice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T15:26:04-07:00","id":649366,"title":"","content":"I see...<br /> <br /> I wonder what kind of guild politics mummies can have, then? If they are awake only for a few months, then they go back to sleep for years, how can there be any politics..? And how can the guilds even function?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T15:29:31-07:00","id":649367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/647250-so-what-is-mummy-about?p=649366#post649366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see...<br /> <br /> I wonder what kind of guild politics mummies can have, then? If they are awake only for a few months, then they go back to sleep for years, how can there be any politics..? And how can the guilds even function?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Guildhalls of the Deathless</i> goes into greater detail, but the short version is: cults with traditions stretching back to ancient Irem go a long way toward providing continuity to the Arisen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T15:29:39-07:00","id":649368,"title":"","content":"The book says that in the case of a rechargeable vessel it can be between four and twenty-six weeks (there's an algorithm based on the dot rating of the relic and dice rolls). It also says that if storytellers want to be a bit stricter with it they can substitute weeks for months or even years. <br /> <br /> So, to summarise, the limit can be anything from once a month to once every 26 years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T15:40:57-07:00","id":649404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/647250-so-what-is-mummy-about?p=648758#post648758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I decided that I'd be very keen on hearing more on the possible Mummy story ideas and the like <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> To get a better feel of the game and all that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a Mummy Actual Play that's been running for a bit over a year. It's one example of what you can do with the game:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/216621-old-gods-of-jakarta-mummy-actual-play\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...my-actual-play</a><br /> <br /> I should point out that Satchel isn't quite correct about the frequency of a Mummy's waking. You don't need to have a relic you personally created to come back with any frequency. You just need one locked into your tomb's Lifeweb. And any Mummy can put a single Guild-appropriate relic into their Lifeweb. Using the mechanics given in the book, there's no reason a Mummy with a one dot relic can't be active for about one year in every two/three.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T16:15:21-07:00","id":649502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/647250-so-what-is-mummy-about?p=649404#post649404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should point out that Satchel isn't quite correct about the frequency of a Mummy's waking. You don't need to have a relic you personally created to come back with any frequency. You just need one locked into your tomb's Lifeweb.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;How Deep the Well&quot; sidebar and the surrounding text says that only a personal relic is merely drained rather than destroyed to make the Call and that such a relic is often a centering relic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T17:51:13-07:00","id":649569,"title":"","content":"A centering relic doesn't have to be a relic the Mummy created. In fact, the Mummy's own possessions in life are listed as relics you can have <i>in addition</i> to the centering relic. My group interpreted that section as reading that any relic the Mummy owns (has put in their Lifeweb, basically) can be used, but I can see how it can be read the other way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T20:52:47-07:00","id":649725,"title":"","content":"Mummy is a game about being the movers and shakers behind the secret history of the world. You are the unliving mysteries at the hearts of international conspiracies that date back before the invention of the written word, and endlessly work the inscrutable will of nameless gods even as you dig through the sands of memory to find your true self. Mummy is a game where you may well work with a foe who killed you a century ago in order to undo a plot of your own doing that's since slipped your mind and has now spiraled out of control due to generations of mistranslation by mere mortals.<br /> <br /> It's a lot of fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T06:25:41-07:00","id":650002,"title":"","content":"Mummy is a game about playing a character who's as old as civilization. It's an exploration of old age - what it means, how people deal with it, etc.<br /> <br /> Mummies are creatures of contradictions. They've seen the birth and death of entire cultures; and yet, they can't remember if they supported the births or brought forth the destructions of nations. When they arise, they have all the power in the world - they can destroy entire cities, if they so choose - but they have so little time to do anything, really. The sand is always running through their fingers, and the irony of a mummy's immortality is that she has to make constant priority calls.<br /> <br /> The powers of the Arisen are vast and glorious and terrible, but also very specific. The Arisen are old testament gods - pillars of fire, plagues, death curses, parting the red sea, that sort of thing. There is a sadness to their vast power - theirs is a kind of magic that is ageless, but it's also static, can't change, and that the world has largely left behind; like the Arisen themselves.<br /> <br /> The Arisen rise into the modern world...and find that nothing fundamental has changed, socially speaking. The downtrodden are still exactly that, and the rich still benefit from exploiting everyone else. The details might be different, but to these creatures who have seen millenia pass, the world is functionally the same as in the culture that created them.<br /> <br /> The Arisen sympathize with those poor and downtrodden - their is an existence of service and slavery that can never, ever end.<br /> <br /> To be Arisen is glorious. Your flesh is immortal. Your spirit seethes with magical power. You have seen the roots of civilization and whisper in their secret language. When your eyes open, they belong to a divine patron, a lord, a god. You\u2019ve seen the gates of the underworld and know for immutable fact that death is not the end of eternal power.<br /> <br /> To be Arisen is terrifying. Your body is a falsehood\u2014a simulated corpse made out of congealed necromancy. You attended the deaths of civilizations, and you can\u2019t remember if you held back the barbarians or put a knife in the emperor\u2019s back. Your eyes are hollow, dry pits; your life signs are a lie you can only tell the world while your true power trickles away. You have seen the gods of the Underworld and know for a fact that death is not the end of eternal service and duty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T06:03:34-07:00","id":652371,"title":"","content":"Perhaps not very ironically, I've found the band Genesis has a couple of good songs to imagine a Mummy's mindset. A typical Arisen story goes along the lines of Tonight, Tonight, Tonight. Very unsure of himself, very guilty feeling, yet full of power and a focus on THIS moment. If you're deceived, In The Air Tonight is your song. Both songs seem to fit how a mummy feels when they wake up, and the psychology they face when they do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T12:05:15-07:00","id":874761,"title":"","content":"Okay then! A few months has passed... and I *still* don't know what a Mummy game could be about.<br /> <br /> I mean, I plan on picking up some NWoD / CoD stuff. I'm considering Mummy, but I'm not sure I want to spend money on a game where the only available story possibility is having the Mummies arise, go for a relic hunt and go to sleep again...<br /> <br /> Help <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T12:15:35-07:00","id":874774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/647250-so-what-is-mummy-about?p=874761#post874761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay then! A few months has passed... and I *still* don't know what a Mummy game could be about.<br /> <br /> I mean, I plan on picking up some NWoD / CoD stuff. I'm considering Mummy, but I'm not sure I want to spend money on a game where the only available story possibility is having the Mummies arise, go for a relic hunt and go to sleep again...<br /> <br /> Help <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>If you can figure out where the block is, maybe we can help. But it's a very Storyteller-driven game at the beginning. Mummies are either awakened with a specific purpose (&quot;Defend the cult&quot;, &quot;Find a relic&quot;, &quot;Move to a new location because this Tomb has been compromised by Mongols/Nazis/Crusaders/ISIS&quot;), because somebody's stolen something from their Tomb, or because of a Sothic Turn.<br /> <br /> There're <i>lots</i> of possible Mummy plots. Start naming a few random things that you'd have other groups do, and we'll say if they're appropriate for Mummy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T12:16:43-07:00","id":874775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/647250-so-what-is-mummy-about?p=874761#post874761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay then! A few months has passed... and I *still* don't know what a Mummy game could be about.<br /> <br /> I mean, I plan on picking up some NWoD / CoD stuff. I'm considering Mummy, but I'm not sure I want to spend money on a game where the only available story possibility is having the Mummies arise, go for a relic hunt and go to sleep again...<br /> <br /> Help <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Mummy can tell far more stories than that. Due to the sheer history Arisen have, and how Memory works, you can easily tell stories of (doomed) love and war, politics and betrayal, forgotten mysteries (by others, and even the mummy themselves), protection (of their cults, of others), and cosmic horrors.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1059\" data-vbnamecard=\"1059\">Azahul</a> has two excellent Actual Plays here on the forums. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/216621-old-gods-of-jakarta-mummy-actual-play\">Old Gods of Jakarta</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/328717-jakarta-by-starlight-deceived-actual-play\">Jakarta By Starlight</a>. Read those. They deal with far more than mere &quot;relic hunt, then sleep&quot; plots.<br /> <br /> I can spin up a few more simple plot ideas, if you need.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T13:50:45-07:00","id":874848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/647250-so-what-is-mummy-about?p=874761#post874761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay then! A few months has passed... and I *still* don't know what a Mummy game could be about.<br /> <br /> I mean, I plan on picking up some NWoD / CoD stuff. I'm considering Mummy, but I'm not sure I want to spend money on a game where the only available story possibility is having the Mummies arise, go for a relic hunt and go to sleep again...<br /> <br /> Help <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>You really enjoyed your time in Palmyra, a pleasant city that enjoyed some prosperity under Seleucid and later Roman rule; your Tomb has been hidden in Syria for the 1,500 years since. Now some idiots are running amok, blowing up all your favorite ruins and causing an ungodly racket. What does an angry god do when he wakes up and finds ISIS making a mess?<br /> <br /> You're awakened by your cult, who you remember as a bunch inoffensive hippies who thought you were a &quot;superior being&quot; from Atlantis that didn't do a whole lot for you during the 70s... and now they've become popular enough to attract a celebrity convert. What was once a peaceful commune is now a retreat for the wealthy, swarmed with paparazzi and fans eager to get in and discover your secrets. How will you scare them off without revealing your unholy true form on live television?<br /> <br /> You came to America in the 1700s, ferried on a vessel paid for by the secret society of wealthy aristocrats who served you at the time, and have been through many Descents in North America in the many years since. A tip-off from your contact in a nearby art museum has allowed you private access to their new collection of Aztec artifacts... and you find your name carved on one of the idols in nearly perfect Iremite. How did they find your name from across the Atlantic, nearly 200 years before you would cross? Hoe sure are you that the past you've been told is true?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T14:03:54-07:00","id":874859,"title":"","content":"You moved to the area last Descent to further one of your projects, and thought you'd be able to continue it in peace. Then you are awakened to defend your cult from a vicious attack upon their compound and your Tomb, and to hunt down and punish the one responsible. The attackers are following so centuries old plan by their ancient god, and you are incensed to think one of your fellows is behind this. But as you find out more, what are you going to do when it turns out it was <i>you</i> who ordered the attack on the area ages ago? And that you've been destroying your own loyal cult?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T14:06:36-07:00","id":874862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you can figure out where the block is, maybe we can help. But it's a very Storyteller-driven game at the beginning. Mummies are either awakened with a specific purpose (&quot;Defend the cult&quot;, &quot;Find a relic&quot;, &quot;Move to a new location because this Tomb has been compromised by Mongols/Nazis/Crusaders/ISIS&quot;), because somebody's stolen something from their Tomb, or because of a Sothic Turn.<br /> <br /> There're <i>lots</i> of possible Mummy plots. Start naming a few random things that you'd have other groups do, and we'll say if they're appropriate for Mummy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, my GM imagination doesn't work that way... I read the game first and see if it inspires any specific ideas. Sometimes, it's easy - with some games, not so.<br /> <br /> For example, I read Mutants &amp; Masterminds and I'm immediately hit with dozens of ideas: I've read enough superhero comics to know what kind of plots I can do in such a game. I read Dark Heresy and, similarly, I get some ideas for stories - the setting presented is rich enough. Moving to NWoD games: Vampire: the Requiem might be a bit hard, but I get the general idea that it's about a twisted, abusive, back-stabbing society of bloodsuckers. I I read Changeling: the Lost and get ideas: True Fae threats, Freehold intrigue, relationship drama and so on.<br /> <br /> I have yet to read Mummy (as I mentioned, I haven't purchased it yet), but I've read about the game. And what I've read leaves me with &quot;Huh, what is there for the players to do&quot;..?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mummy can tell far more stories than that. Due to the sheer history Arisen have, and how Memory works, you can easily tell stories of (doomed) love and war, politics and betrayal, forgotten mysteries (by others, and even the mummy themselves), protection (of their cults, of others), and cosmic horrors.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1059\" data-vbnamecard=\"1059\">Azahul</a> has two excellent Actual Plays here on the forums. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/216621-old-gods-of-jakarta-mummy-actual-play\">Old Gods of Jakarta</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/328717-jakarta-by-starlight-deceived-actual-play\">Jakarta By Starlight</a>. Read those. They deal with far more than mere &quot;relic hunt, then sleep&quot; plots.<br /> <br /> I can spin up a few more simple plot ideas, if you need.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha! Please do <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You moved to the area last Descent to further one of your projects, and thought you'd be able to continue it in peace. Then you are awakened to defend your cult from a vicious attack upon their compound and your Tomb, and to hunt down and punish the one responsible. The attackers are following so centuries old plan by their ancient god, and you are incensed to think one of your fellows is behind this. But as you find out more, what are you going to do when it turns out it was <i>you</i> who ordered the attack on the area ages ago? And that you've been destroying your own loyal cult? </div> </div> </div>Here's a question: what would a Mummy's &quot;project&quot; be, actually? What are the goals of these characters? What do they work towards?<br /> <br /> I mean, the Kindred hunt and plot. Werewolves kill invading spirits. Changelings hide from the True Fae. What do Mummies do? Whe I was reading up on the game, I learned that they hunt down relics or attack tomb raiders. They don't seem to have any other goals...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You really enjoyed your time in Palmyra, a pleasant city that enjoyed some prosperity under Seleucid and later Roman rule; your Tomb has been hidden in Syria for the 1,500 years since. Now some idiots are running amok, blowing up all your favorite ruins and causing an ungodly racket. What does an angry god do when he wakes up and finds ISIS making a mess?<br /> <br /> You're awakened by your cult, who you remember as a bunch inoffensive hippies who thought you were a &quot;superior being&quot; from Atlantis that didn't do a whole lot for you during the 70s... and now they've become popular enough to attract a celebrity convert. What was once a peaceful commune is now a retreat for the wealthy, swarmed with paparazzi and fans eager to get in and discover your secrets. How will you scare them off without revealing your unholy true form on live television?<br /> <br /> You came to America in the 1700s, ferried on a vessel paid for by the secret society of wealthy aristocrats who served you at the time, and have been through many Descents in North America in the many years since. A tip-off from your contact in a nearby art museum has allowed you private access to their new collection of Aztec artifacts... and you find your name carved on one of the idols in nearly perfect Iremite. How did they find your name from across the Atlantic, nearly 200 years before you would cross? Hoe sure are you that the past you've been told is true?</div> </div> </div> </div>These help, thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1245,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","user":"Varsovian","date":". 04-26-2016, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T14:29:53-07:00","id":874884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/647250-so-what-is-mummy-about?p=874862#post874862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a question: what would a Mummy's &quot;project&quot; be, actually? What are the goals of these characters? What do they work towards?<br /> <br /> I mean, the Kindred hunt and plot. Werewolves kill invading spirits. Changelings hide from the True Fae. What do Mummies do? Whe I was reading up on the game, I learned that they hunt down relics or attack tomb raiders. They don't seem to have any other goals...</div> </div> </div> </div>What are their projects? Whatever they wish. For immortals, it helps to have long term activities to keep one occupied.<br /> <br /> The Tef-Aabhi plan out architectural (and, for the Flesh-Masons, bloodline) plans to concentrate Heka. The Mesen-Nebu continually seek to improve things, adding to their collections, amassing power for their Cults, adding more beauty to their surroundings, etc. The Maa-Kep manipulate from behind the scenes and help others with their labors, sometimes just making sure everything stays together. The Sesha-Hebsu are scribes and researchers, investigating mysteries and compiling knowledge. The Su-Menent maintain tradition and guard secrets and horrors best lost to time.<br /> <br /> But even besides Guild motivations, any individual Mummy might want revenge on a rival, to create a monument to their Judge, seek the answer to an enigma encountered in a previous Descent, grow their cult to new heights, advance their status (in either Guild or Nome), or just help out a friend (or their descendants, should they have passed away in the mean time).<br /> <br /> The character's Judge also presides over something, and forwarding that also offers a longer Descent.<br /> <br /> And then, of course, there is Apotheosis...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T14:50:33-07:00","id":874907,"title":"","content":"Thanks!<br /> <br /> See, I didn't know that Mummies might have any long-term projects... From what I read, Mummies wake up for short periods and might spend decades inactive. So, how does one plan anything when &quot;living&quot; like that? Also, it seemed to me that they were rather passive characters, waking up merely on behalf of their cults or the Judges...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T15:42:04-07:00","id":874950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/647250-so-what-is-mummy-about?p=874907#post874907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks!<br /> <br /> See, I didn't know that Mummies might have any long-term projects... From what I read, Mummies wake up for short periods and might spend decades inactive. So, how does one plan anything when &amp;quot;living&amp;quot; like that? Also, it seemed to me that they were rather passive characters, waking up merely on behalf of their cults or the Judges...</div> </div> </div> </div>They cannot awaken under their own power. But the Cult is modeled as a series of merits, similar to...Sanctum, I guess? You pour points into it and choose what those points mean. So the Cult is another player and Storyteller tool.<br /> <br /> Also, Arisen plans take time. Eugenics, architecture, excavations, tracking down relics... These things can take lifetimes. In a game I ran for my wife, her Mummy started looking for a ruin in the 1300s and ended up across the Atlantic in the 1700s before she finally found it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T16:54:50-07:00","id":875002,"title":"","content":"Remember that beneath the awesome power and fading memories, Mummies are still people. They still have thoughts and feelings and opinions which drive them. After the first rush of the Descent, an Arisen begins to remember who they are, what they have done in the past, and how their current actions may (or may not) fit into a broader pattern. On Sothic Turns, or when an Arisen has completed its First Purpose, it may have time to explore its own interests. Those interests can be just as diverse as any human. The actions of an Arisen who fought alongside the Spartacus Rebellion, urged its Cult to participate in the French Revolution, and ultimately relocated to a suburb in England where it spent the 60s and 70s trying to foster a Communist commune may have its own ideas of how to spend its free time once it awakens 40 years later to a tiny cult of mostly disillusioned academics than, say, a religious fanatic of the Su-Menent whose cultists have always ridden a wave of fundamentalist religion to encourage new recruits. Indeed, these two may be rivals who have clashed time and again over the course of history, and have long-running plots to undermine the other and steal their relics.<br /> <br /> More generally though, I encourage you to consider Cults as a big offshoot of the Mummy. The character of the Cult and its objectives are going to play a big role. A Cult can awake a Mummy and give it a purpose, any purpose, not just &quot;chase this relic&quot;. Consequently, a Mummy's purpose might be anything its Cult wants. Gang-based cults might wake up a heavy hitter for a land grab, a corporate cult may wake its &quot;primary asset&quot; to wield control over fate and the minds of others to help in a hostile takeover, a small family-based cult may wake their god simply because tradition demands that the Arisen bear witness to the sacred union between two members. Because the Cult drives the purpose, an Arisen can be given an objective of literally anything their thoroughly human followers might want, which runs the full gamut of the human experience. Cursed Necropolis DC had some interesting ideas on how those cults might be influenced in turn by the Arisen's objectives (cultists in airport customs are hot property), so it's not a one-way street either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T18:14:33-07:00","id":875078,"title":"","content":"One other fun thing to consider: a Mummy chronicle can easily consist of switching between playing one of the Arisen and one or more mortals, be they loyal cultists, rival sorcerers, or angry hunters. In a game that already heavily incentivizes flashbacks in play, alternating perspectives fits and allows for new angles on the plot from the perspective of someone who isn't an amnesiac Egyptian slave/god.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T18:15:04-07:00","id":875079,"title":"","content":"I see. Thanks for the replies, it really broadened my view of the game!<br /> <br /> I might end up buying this after all... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T19:03:01-07:00","id":875106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/647250-so-what-is-mummy-about?p=874907#post874907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks!<br /> <br /> See, I didn't know that Mummies might have any long-term projects... From what I read, Mummies wake up for short periods and might spend decades inactive. So, how does one plan anything when &quot;living&quot; like that? Also, it seemed to me that they were rather passive characters, waking up merely on behalf of their cults or the Judges...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How do they plan? With redundancies. And delegation. Mummies (typically?) create the plan, then have their Cults carry out the necessary action as they &quot;sleep&quot;. Hopefully, the Cult sticks to the plan, and doesn't distort or subvert it over time. The mummy might leave instructions to wake the periodically to adjust and plot out the next phases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T21:00:50-07:00","id":875228,"title":"","content":"Here's another suggestion if you are unsure about Mummy... start your game with the Assassination of Franz Ferdinand. The themes that have been associated with World War 1 are similar to those of Mummy. The elite of an empire who do not understand that the world has moved on from their time and that their traditions are no longer relevant. Decades of carefully laid plans, torn up not by the Wrath of God, but by the wrath of artillery barrages. Friends, allies, and support networks called away to fight a pointless war that can't be won with little chance of ever returning home. <br /> <br /> Swap between the story of the Mummies and the stories of their cultists, both in the trenches and &quot;safe&quot; at home. Watch as the mortal dilemmas mirrors those of the immortals. <br /> <br /> Also, Mummies can be active from anywhere from a couple months if they are brash and unwise, to several years if they are prudent and lucky. Unless a Mummy dies multiple times, they should be active for about 380 days if they descend as quickly as (in)humanly possible. Mummies also earn descent resets by taking the following actions:<ul><li>Creating great monuments to Irem</li> <li>Destroying greater Amkhat</li> <li>Punishing those who violate their tombs</li> <li>Dedicating the deaths of rivals to the Judges in front of witnesses</li> <li>Saving the unlives of mummies of the same judge</li> </ul>Each of these can be motive enough when a Mummy has no immediate purpose. More importantly, these restart the waning of Sekhem. If you're at Sekhem 1, that means you get another 180 days before you have to pick up the dice again. The Mummy's experience alternates between careful planning and frantic work, but a smart Mummy can last years at Sekhem 1 if they pick their battles carefully and don't piss off the judges. There are Mummies who cannonically made it all the way through WW1. They still aren't active for long periods of time, but most probably get a couple of years instead of a couple of months.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T21:12:31-07:00","id":875240,"title":"","content":"A similarly exciting flashpoint: the Arab Spring. While the power structures in North Africa and the Middle East are young to the Arisen, these were powerful nations brought low and reshaped by the common people, using brand-new technologies that didn't exist a mere few decades ago. As protests turn into clashes with police and then the military, old Cults draw upon their Arisen patrons to help turn the tide or just survive the chaos. What does it mean to the Deathless to see the common man, the laborers and common folk that likely echo their societal role when they lived as mortals so long ago, rise up and overthrow their rightful leaders? What do explosive bullets, jet fighters, and Twitter mean to creatures of bronze and papyrus? Do they attempt to prop up the failing old governments, shape the rising new order, or try to carve out petty kingdoms in the war-torn madness of Libya and Syria, ruling openly for the first time in centuries?<br /> <br /> One year later, the Sothic Turn hits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}